module

public import CORALean.ContSet.Ellipsoid.Real.Theorems.MemConstructIff
public import CORALean.ContSet.Conversion.Real.Operations.Ellipsoid_to_SpectraShadow
public import CORALean.ContSet.Ellipsoid.Real.Theorems.ConstructSubsetOfLe
public import CORALean.ContSet.Ellipsoid.Real.Theorems.ConstructOfFactor
public import CORALean.Global.EuclideanNorm
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef

@[expose] public section

/-!
# The Schur form is the ellipsoid

`A₀ + Σᵢ xᵢ Aᵢ = [[1, yᵀ], [y, Q]]` at `y = x - q`, whose quadratic form at `(a, z)` is
`a² + 2a (y·z) + zᵀ Q z`: nonnegative for all `a` iff `(y·z)² ≤ zᵀ Q z`, the minimum over `a` being
at `a = -(y·z)`, that is iff `y yᵀ ⪯ Q`. That is `y = G w` with `‖w‖₂ ≤ 1`: one way
`(y·z)² = (w·G z)² ≤ ‖G z‖₂² = zᵀ Q z` by Cauchy–Schwarz, the other `y` lies in the ellipsoid of
`y yᵀ`, generated by `y` itself, which the larger `Q` contains (`construct_subset_of_le`). For every
positive semi-definite `Q`, degenerate ones included.
-/

